"""Tabular candidate feature store: information the averaged baseline does not use or uses only coarsely, generated by family. Key MVT_ID_mvt,
covering all DEP rows (12 training months + ranking). Labels do not take part (BLOCK only takes the in-block time of ARR rows, which is available on the
same basis for the test set); label-dependent smoothed target encodings (TE) are not computed here but per fold in the CV script.

Families (column prefixes):
- a_: unused columns - FLIGHT_RULE (mvt/flt), callsign != flight number, callsign letter suffix, aircraft type flt != mvt, ADES_FILED != ADES, ADEP_flt != ADEP,
      digits and number of digits of the flight number, pairing of FLIGHT_ID with an ARR row at another challenge airport (a_pair) and the air-time deviation
      of paired rows (a_pair_air_dev = landing at the destination - take-off here - route median).
- b_: physical - stand coordinates (merged OSM and apt.dat table) as planar coordinates relative to the airport reference point, straight-line distance from stand
      to the end of the runway in use, shortest path length and detour ratio from stand to runway end on the apt.dat taxi network (1201/1202, runway edges removed);
      stand letter prefix (apron) and number; median taxi-in of ARR rows by stand / apron (all files, transductive);
      median MVT-AOBT_3 of non-synthetic matched rows by (airport, stand, runway) and (airport, stand) (transductive; stand-level prior of the NM-side taxi time).
- c_: operating state observable in the test period - number of aircraft in the system (SCHED+10min / EOBT+5min passed but not departed), number of aircraft on the
      ground at MVT-15min whose AOBT_3-to-MVT interval covers that time (airport / own runway), departures in the previous 30 minutes and within +-30 minutes on the
      own runway, airport departures within +-30 minutes and the own-runway share, number of active departure / arrival runways within +-30 minutes and configuration id,
      own-runway arrivals within +-15 minutes, mean MVT-SCHED of other airport departures within +-30 minutes, mean taxi-in excess of arrivals in the previous 60 minutes
      on the own apron; own-runway backlog (SCHED+10min / EOBT+5min passed, not departed) and mean MVT-SCHED and MVT-EOBT within +-30 minutes on the own runway;
      stall indicators (largest departure gap in the previous 60 minutes on the runway / airport, seconds since the end of the last gap > 10 minutes)
      - motivation: the remaining shared residual sits at the level of runway x day x hour, mostly in class C.
- d_: turnaround chain and flight number (label-free parts) - arrival delay of the previous arrival at the same stand (in-block - scheduled, landing - scheduled),
      scheduled turnaround time, flag for inbound flight number +-1, whether the inbound origin is a challenge airport; the inbound flight chained by "same airline,
      flight number +-1, in-block 10 min to 12 h before MVT" (any stand): gap, delay, same stand or not;
      MVT-SCHED of the same flight number on the previous / next day, same stand / same runway or not; month mean (excluding itself) of MVT-SCHED and of
      non-synthetic MVT-AOBT_3 for the same flight number, number of flights in the month. Also outputs the TE key k_cs (callsign).
- e_: local time (airport time zone, with daylight saving) hour, minute, weekday, scheduled local hour; public holidays (entered by hand per country / region for 2025 and
      the 2026 test months) and the day before / after.
Usage: .venv/bin/python build_tabular_features.py raw n2/feat.parquet /path/to/ext/xplane-apt out/pf.parquet
Memory: 2.43 M DEP rows + about 2.4 M ARR rows with only the needed columns, peak about 3 GB.
"""
import datetime as dt
import os
import re
import sys

import numpy as np
import polars as pl
from scipy.sparse import coo_matrix
from scipy.sparse.csgraph import connected_components, dijkstra

os.environ.setdefault('POLARS_UNKNOWN_EXTENSION_TYPE_BEHAVIOR', 'load_as_storage')
RAW, FEAT, XP, OUT = sys.argv[1:5]
FILES = sorted(f for f in os.listdir(RAW) if f.startswith('training_')) + ['ranking.parquet']
APTS = ['EDDF', 'EDDM', 'EGLL', 'EHAM', 'LEBL', 'LEMD', 'LFPG', 'LIRF', 'LSZH', 'LTFM']
TZ = {'EDDF': 'Europe/Berlin', 'EDDM': 'Europe/Berlin', 'EGLL': 'Europe/London', 'EHAM': 'Europe/Amsterdam', 'LEBL': 'Europe/Madrid',
      'LEMD': 'Europe/Madrid', 'LFPG': 'Europe/Paris', 'LIRF': 'Europe/Rome', 'LSZH': 'Europe/Zurich', 'LTFM': 'Europe/Istanbul'}
SH = np.int64(1) << np.int64(40)


def log(*x):
    print(*x, flush=True)


def ep(c):
    return pl.col(c).dt.epoch('s')


# ---------------- Public holidays (entered by hand; region = state / autonomous community of the airport; weak feature only) ----------------
